                {
                    "name": "create new requirements",
                    "description": "<p>While a user doesn't have to select the user types that apply to the requirement, they must still give it a name. If they do no select any users, the name defaults to \"Users can...\"</p><p>Next, they can optionally provide a rich-text description for elaboration and a source to trace where requirements have come from (such as other documents, meetings, etc.)</p><p>If a requirement is blocked, the user can mark it as such by giving it a reason.</p><p>A \"Quick Add\" button should be available at all times where the user can create a requirement and specify the feature it belongs to, instead of using a button within the feature itself.</p>",
